  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\nCompound IV is a carboxylic acid whereas others are alcohols. So IV is most acidic, amongst the alcohols. Presence of $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ increases acidic strength while the presence of $-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ lowers. Amongst I and III, more acidic is $\\mathrm{I}$ as $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ exerts it's $-\\mathrm{R}$ influence in para position.",
